<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 07_colors/20: Opacity versus alpha -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Opacity versus alpha</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .pair { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, #e2e8f0 0 10px, #fff 10px 20px); }
    .pair div { flex: 1; padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 10px; font-weight: 700; }
    .faded { background: #7c3aed; color: #fff; opacity: 0.5; }
    .alpha { background: rgb(124 58 237 / 0.5); color: #fff; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Opacity versus alpha</h1>
    <p class="lead">opacity fades a whole element; an alpha colour fades only its background.</p>
    <div class="pair">
      <div class="faded">opacity: 0.5 &mdash; the text fades too</div>
      <div class="alpha">rgb(&hellip; / 0.5) &mdash; crisp text</div>
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
